{"key":"CardsWindow","text":"## CardsWindow\n\nThe **Cards Window** is a card-game construction suite. Build a deck by\nslicing a sprite sheet into cards, then lay them out and play on a virtual\ntable — deal, flip, shuffle, and arrange stacks. It's a set of tools for\nmaking card games, not a single editor.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.03 | The ☰ menu holds Save, Export (download), Shuffle, Deal, and View Extents. The ⊞ Deck Editor button opens the deck builder.\nTable Canvas | 0.50, 0.52 | The play surface. Click an exposed card to flip it; click a covered card to bring it to front (peel a stack). Drag to move; drag empty space to box-select; Ctrl/Cmd+Click to add to a selection. Right-click a card, a stack, or the table for actions.\n\n---\n\n### Table\n\n- **Click** an exposed card — flip it face up / down\n- **Click** a covered card — bring it to front (so you can peel a stack one card at a time)\n- **Drag** a card or selection — move it\n- **Drag empty space** — box-select multiple cards\n- **Ctrl/Cmd + Click** — add / remove a card from the selection\n- **Right-click** — context menu for the card, the stack, or the whole table (Shuffle, Deal, View Extents, Save, Export)\n\n### Deck Editor  (⊞ button)\n\n- **Load Sheet** — pick a sprite sheet image\n- **Grid** — drag the orange offset handles and cyan padding handles, or choose a preset, to slice the sheet into cards; a live preview shows the cell under the cursor\n- Assign each cell a rank / suit, then **Confirm Deck**\n- **Export Deck** — download the deck as JSON\n\n### Shortcuts\n\n- **Ctrl/Cmd + Click** — additive multi-select on the table\n- **Drag (empty area)** — box-select\n- **Right-click** — context menus (table / card / stack)\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: GameDesign\n\n---","screenshot":""}